Termux Usage Guide
==================

Termux is a terminal emulator and Linux environment for Android.

INSTALLATION
------------
Download Termux from F-Droid (recommended) or Google Play Store.

BASIC COMMANDS
--------------
pkg update            - Update package list
pkg upgrade           - Upgrade installed packages
pkg install <name>    - Install a package
pkg uninstall <name>  - Remove a package
pkg list-installed    - List installed packages
pkg search <name>     - Search for packages

COMMON PACKAGES
---------------
pkg install python    - Install Python
pkg install nodejs    - Install Node.js
pkg install git       - Install Git
pkg install vim       - Install Vim editor
pkg install curl      - Install curl
pkg install wget      - Install wget
pkg install openssh   - Install SSH client/server
pkg install nano      - Install nano editor

FILE SYSTEM
-----------
~                     - Home directory (/data/data/com.termux/files/home)
/sdcard               - Internal storage access
termux-setup-storage  - Grant storage permissions

STORAGE ACCESS
--------------
Run: termux-setup-storage
Then access phone storage at: ~/storage/

GIT USAGE
---------
git clone <url>       - Clone a repository
git add .             - Stage all changes
git commit -m "msg"   - Commit changes
git push              - Push to remote
git pull              - Pull from remote

PYTHON USAGE
------------
python3 --version     - Check Python version
pip install <pkg>     - Install Python package
python3 script.py     - Run a Python script

SSH
---
ssh-keygen -t ed25519 - Generate SSH key
cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub  - View public key (add to GitHub)
ssh user@host         - Connect to remote server

USEFUL TIPS
-----------
- Use Ctrl+L to clear the screen
- Use Tab for auto-completion
- Long press on screen to copy/paste
- Swipe from left edge to open extra keys bar
- Use 'termux-open <file>' to open files with Android apps
- Multiple sessions: swipe from left or use Volume Down + Q

KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
------------------
Ctrl+C  - Cancel current command
Ctrl+D  - Exit session
Ctrl+Z  - Suspend process
Ctrl+A  - Move to start of line
Ctrl+E  - Move to end of line
